    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that the derivative of the {@link Sigmoid} function vanishes for arguments far from the origin. <p>A sigmoid saturates towards its asymptotes as the input grows in either direction, so its slope (the first derivative) tends to zero. This test feeds a range of large positive and negative inputs—including the extreme values {@code ±Double.MAX_VALUE} and {@code ±Infinity}—and checks that the computed derivative is exactly {@code 0}.</p>"
